\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces AIME-24 at budget 2048 (subset scale: 30 problems $\times $ 4 seeds; own reference bank at $0.371$). Free-running separates the three policies ($0.283$ / $0.217$ / $0.142$); their readout accuracies are \emph  {identical} at $0.462$ --- same correctness on every one of the 93 conditions where an answer boundary is defined (27 of the 120 are undefined for every press), with 85 of those 93 converging to the same extracted answer through visibly different generations. Held-trace evaluation cannot see the difference between these policies at all; no press approaches the reference (no $>$100\% regime \emph  {in this cell}, which is 7B; the 8B published-configuration cell is reported in \cref  {sec:threats}).}}{22}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:aime}{{7}{22}{AIME-24 at budget 2048 (subset scale: 30 problems $\times $ 4 seeds; own reference bank at $0.371$). Free-running separates the three policies ($0.283$ / $0.217$ / $0.142$); their readout accuracies are \emph {identical} at $0.462$ --- same correctness on every one of the 93 conditions where an answer boundary is defined (27 of the 120 are undefined for every press), with 85 of those 93 converging to the same extracted answer through visibly different generations. Held-trace evaluation cannot see the difference between these policies at all; no press approaches the reference (no $>$100\% regime \emph {in this cell}, which is 7B; the 8B published-configuration cell is reported in \cref {sec:threats})}{figure.caption.17}{}}
\newlabel{fig:aime@cref}{{[figure][7][]7}{[1][21][]22}{}{}{}}
